''Who's the commanding officer? Ain't you!?''
In order to allow IJA officers and NCOs to be identified by troops while not drawing attention from enemy snipers, some common items like packs of cigarettes or playing cards were attached to helmets. Exact rules differed from unit to unit, with SNLF detachments ignoring this convention altogether.
