''Bushido is realized in the presence of death.''

Type 98 pants, with weeds and branches inserted into puttees. While Japanese used unconventional tactics, their use contradicted the Bushido code on which IJA was built. Soldiers and officers preferred to hold positions to their death rather than retreat to live another day.
